+- `workspace-write` (logon SID, Everyone, workspace SID, temp SID): the workspace and the session's PRIVATE temp subdirectory carry separate Write grants; other ACL-addressable writes are denied except for the documented Everyone and hard-link boundaries. The workspace grant is a TWO-ACE pair: an inherit-only `(OI|CI|IO)` full-`GRANT_MASK` ACE (descendants keep Write+Delete for delete/rename/git) and a root-only `ROOT_GRANT_MASK` ACE (no DELETE, no FILE_DELETE_CHILD) — the workspace ROOT object itself cannot be deleted or renamed by the confined child. Root DELETION also requires FILE_DELETE_CHILD on the parent, so a parent that grants the caller (its own user ACE or an ambient Everyone-style ACE) remains the documented partial boundary; the command guard's disaster tier is the primary root-deletion defense. Pre-split single-ACE grants are migrated in place on first provision (one revoke+pair merge).
